      "id": 1,
      "text": "Franklin County was organized on January 15, 1851, and named after the American polymath Benjamin Franklin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin_County%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The county seat, Hampton, hosts the historic Franklin County Courthouse, built in 1891 and listed on the National Register in 1976.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin_County%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every mid‑July, the Franklin County Fair turns the west side of Hampton into a five‑day celebration featuring rodeo, concerts, and figure‑8 races.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27,
        28,
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin_County%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The fairgrounds also house the Franklin County Historical Museum, a turn‑of‑the‑century village called Pleasant Hill with old‑west shows and music.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin_County%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Grandpa's Farm on the fairgrounds demonstrates every phase of farming, from draft‑horse‑powered implements to antique tractors and steam engines.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
